A||N||14||Lisa 86 2m4||Installing Keyless Entry||||5||
Z||000000||Lisa 86 2m4||12-29-2000||08:27 PM||||Hi all!<BR>I'm in the process of installing keyless entry and thought I should ask a few questions before proceeding... I got directions off Virtual Fiero, but still have some questions.  The trunk relay wires placed near the steering column are said by VF to be Gray, Black and Tan.  The wires I am looking at are yellow, black and tan. Am I looking at the right wires? If so, which wire would be the 'gray' one that hooks to the remote's wire?<BR>This system also comes with the capability to lock/unlock via the ignition switch, is it a pain to get to the ignition switch 12V brown wire? And finally, the wires from the keyless I have attached to my car's lock relay wires by peeling back the insulation of the car's wire and wrapping the wire of the system around the exposed area, will this make a viable connection? Oh, and 1 more, into the lock relay's there were 2 black wires, and 2 blue wires, I only spliced into one of each, is that correct?<BR>Thanks all!! Be forewarned, next I'm putting in driving lights!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||MoneypitGT||12-29-2000||10:44 PM||||As far as I know there are isn't a trunk release relay, it is a direct switch, but either way it doesn't matter...The fastest way to do a keyless is to pull the center console, like you would to gain access to the ECM. There is a large wire loom that runs to the left (if facing the ECM) that will contain all of your wires except for your locks, but sounds like you already found them. The relays have two of each wire, either one will do, doesn't matter. The igntion is Pink (12ga), Constant power is Red (12ga), parking lights will be brown and as far as the trunk relase goes I think it is white but not 100%, if you have a meter you can easily find out. Also another note, everything is a + trigger so you will need relays, not all keyless entrys have them built in.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||skitime||12-29-2000||10:53 PM||||I just look at mine and I spliced into the black and white (maybe black and tan) wire from the relay which it located under the dash to the right of the steering column.  I did not connect to anything near the ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||12-30-2000||12:09 AM||||Where's the best place to get a key-less entry set-up?<P>I want it bad. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Lisa 86 2m4||12-30-2000||09:16 AM||||I ordered my keyless entry system from JC Whitney, and if you go to the Mich Fiero club page they have detailed instructions on installing this particular system, its' the Model 2RTA. It's on sale now at JC for 29.99, which I thought was a great price.||||reg||1
