Z||000006||fropuff||12-30-2000||12:35 PM||||That's a good price.  I'll have to get one myself.  Does this one have a huge remote control?  I don't care for those ones.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfixit58||12-30-2000||02:35 PM||||I installed one in my 87 GT a couple of weeks ago. It's from Bulldog Security but I'm sure most are simular. I was able to install mine without cutting a single wire. What I did instead was to find each wire and remove it from the plastic connector housing then, solder the relay's wire to the end of the pin (the metal connector) then just snap it back into the plastic connector.<P>To remove the metal connector from the plastic housing, simply slide a small rigid wire between the metal connector (connection end) and the plastic housing (This will disengage the locking tab) then pull the wire. You may have to flatten the rigid wire a bit and twist it around but keep working it and it'll come loose.<P>For the trunk, I believe it was the black wire with the white stripe. The relay is mounted to the steering column on the right side. <P>For the locks, I used the same method. The connector with the locks is located behind the driver's side kick panel. There are two different wires - one each for the left and right. Light blue and black I think.<P>Again, I just removed the metal connector from it's plactic holder (commonly called the connector) and soldered the wire to the metal connector pin. I chose not to use the ignition cutoff relay.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000008||Lisa 86 2m4||12-30-2000||03:20 PM||||I tried so hard to get the wires out of the connector harness, but was just too afraid of breaking something, I wish I had known how easy it could have been!! I haven't hooked up the battery cable yet to try it out, but the system is completely installed. <BR>The remotes for this system are actually quite small and have 3 buttons. The system came with 2 remotes. <BR>Thanks everybody for taking time to help me out!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Lisa 86 2m4||12-30-2000||06:46 PM||||Well, just hooked the battery back up, and the only the unlock works.  Shoot! Can I figure out what I did wrong? No.  I guess it's time to sell my tools!||||reg||1
Z||000010||BOILERMAKER||12-30-2000||07:55 PM||||It just takes patience.  I did the same job and ended up splicing into the wiring harness right next to the fuse box behind the carpet.  Wasn't a big deal, but I haven't tried the harness around the ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfixit58||12-31-2000||12:47 PM||||Lisa,<P>I believe the "lock" and "unlock" use different wires. Like I mentioned in my previous post, I believe the wire colors are light blue and black on the kick panel connectors.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierogod1||01-01-2001||03:02 PM|||| On the trunk switch just use a test light (with the swith pluged in) to see what wire has power when you press the opener. Do you have factory power locks? I just installed an Autocomand romote start keyless system in a freinds 86Se. The door locks did not work.<BR>I pulled the door lock motors apart and cleaned them. I also cleaned the door latchs.<BR>It worked well! This was the first one i have installed in a fiero but it won't be the last. My little sis gets one in her Fiero. You can also go to Designtech's homepage they will e-mail you a complete install sheet for the fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Lisa 86 2m4||01-04-2001||05:41 PM||||Well, my latest update is this...contrary to the Mich Fiero instructions on the JC Whitney 2RTA model, if not using the purple wire(to ignitions) it should simply be capped off, not tied in anywhere. So now, the lock/unlock works-I just have to finish replacing the lock cylinders-ick! However, I am unable to get the trunk switch to work. The instructions tell how to hook up if there are two wires, but mine has 3. Brown, yellow, and black.  I have found that with the ignition on, brown has constant current, yellow has constant current and black has no current. With the ignition off, all run current if the trunk release is activated, therefore, I tied in the remote to the black wire, but to no avail. Any ideas? The remote has two wire for the trunk, orange and brown. Brown is the polar wire that I connected to the remotes' 12v, perhaps it should be grounded?<BR>*Apparently, Fiero's require an added selonoid for the trunk release to work.*<BR>Still tickled it's halfway there, though!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Lisa 86 2m4 (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||fiero56||01-04-2001||06:00 PM||||Make sure if you are trying to use it with the ignition in, the parking brake has to be on.||||reg||1
